message.content:
The fuzzer just calls `h->read(&i)` for each handler. It doesn't do any painting. So the crash must happen during the `read()` call itself.

But the crash stack shows `destStoreMonoLsb` → `blend_untransformed_generic` → `fillRect_normalized`. This is the painter pipeline. So the `read()` function must be using `QPainter` internally.

Looking at the XCF handler's `copyLayerToImage`:
```cpp
if (copy == copyRGBToRGB && layer.apply_mask != 1) {
    QPainter painter(&image);
    painter.setOpacity(layer.opacity / 255.0);
    painter.setCompositionMode(QPainter::CompositionMode_Source);
    painter.drawImage(x + layer.x_offset, y + layer.y_offset, layer.image_tiles[j][i]);
    continue;
}
```

This uses `QPainter` to draw the tile onto the image. But this shortcut is only for `copyRGBToRGB`, which is for RGB layer types.

